initialIdeals -- calls gfan and returns the list of initial ideals
******************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        initialIdeals(I)
  * Inputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal
  * Outputs:
      * the list of initial ideals of I.  Note that each initial ideal is given
        as a list of monomial generators in ring(I), not as a monomial ideal.

Description
===========

Given an ideal I in M2, this function calls gfan and returns the list of
initial ideals of I.
+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b];                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a^2+b^2,a*b);       |
|                                   |
|o2 : Ideal of R                    |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : initialIdeals(I)              |
|                                   |
|             2   3          2   3  |
|o3 = {{a*b, a , b }, {a*b, b , a }}|
|                                   |
|o3 : List                          |
+-----------------------------------+

Ways to use initialIdeals:
==========================

  * "initialIdeals(Ideal)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note initialIdeals: initialIdeals, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

