polymakeStatePolytope(Ideal) -- computes the state polytope of an ideal
***********************************************************************

  * Function: *note polymakeStatePolytope: polymakeStatePolytope,
  * Usage: 
        statePolytope(I)
  * Inputs:
      * an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the list of vertices of the state
        polytope

Description
===========

See Sturmfels's book Groebner bases and convex polytopes, page 14 for the
                                                                         
definition of State(I).  (The difference between this and State (I) is that for
                                                               m               
all sufficiently large m, State (I) does not distinguish between initial ideals
                               m
which have the same saturation with regard to the irrelevant ideal, whereas in
State(I), these are separated.)
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a..d];                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal(a*c-b^2,a*d-b*c,b*d-c^2);                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : polymakeStatePolytope(I)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = {{11, 7, 7, 11}, {7, 15, 3, 11}, {4, 18, 6, 8}, {3, 18, 9, 6}, {11, 3,  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     15, 7}, {8, 6, 18, 4}, {6, 9, 18, 3}, {3, 15, 15, 3}}                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note polymakeStatePolytope(Ideal): polymakeStatePolytope_lpIdeal_rp, --
    computes the state polytope of an ideal
